\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Verifier error model}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{verifier}
\tag{reward}

\p{Let #{S\in\{0,1\}} denote success under the independent criterion and let
#{V\in\{0,1\}} be the verifier decision used during training. The verifier's
\strong{false-positive} and \strong{false-negative} rates are}

##{
  \alpha=\Pr(V=1\mid S=0),\qquad
  \beta=\Pr(V=0\mid S=1).
}

\p{This is an FTIP application of the binary measurement-error model. Section
2.2 of \citef{guo2025deepseek} uses exact-answer or rule-based checks in
particular domains. The abstraction allows those checks to be
imperfect relative to the capability that the independent evaluator intends
to measure.}

\p{The pair #{(\alpha,\beta)} is conditional on the task and generated
trajectory distribution. It need not remain fixed as the policy learns to
search for checker weaknesses.}
